> 1. recently some thread mentioned alt.org/nethack and these ttrec
> session files. can somebody tell me how to play these files on
> windows? programs i need to download to do this?  i searched around a
> little bit, but to no avail...

It is available with ttyrec, <http://namazu.org/
~satoru/ttyrec/index.html.en>, there is also a Java player there, 
<http://kakugawa.aial.hiroshima-u.ac.jp/misc/ttyplayer/index-en.shtml>.

I don't know of a ttyplay binary for Windows though, if that is what you 
want.

You can watch games on the alt.org server if you log in, you don't need 
any extra software (besides your telnet client) for this.

> 2. how do you play slash'em the "nethack-way" with ascii-graphics
> (IBM-graphics) and without mouse controlled menues? i suppose via some
> commands in the options file but i couldn't figure out the right
> syntax.

One question at a time:
* ASCII-graphics
  Select 'Map' menu and any ASCII choice.
* IBM-graphics
  'O' for options and then 'm' for IBM-graphics.
* without mouse controlled menus
  This can't be changed ingame, set it in defaults.nh.
* defaults.nh line for all of the above
  OPTIONS=map_mode:ascii8x12,IBMgraphics, windowtype:tty

/Kristoffer

